# Health and memories as chains (doc 62, phase 7). One speaker starts, as they are (an old wolf's knees, a miner's
# chest, a pup's wobbly tooth; a widow's memory, a Frosthollow wolf far from the snow), and the other answers as THEY
# are (health.answer, memories.answer: the healer prescribes, the nervy step back, the old outdo, the frank
# contradict), and the first has the last word (health.back, memories.back). The ailing are remembered for three
# days, so a friend can ask after it; old times told together are remembered by the pair.
#
# Reviewed 2026-10-13. What kind of thing was said is remembered for the chain, so the answers suit it:
#   health:   pair.mem.hk = sick (catching), tired, hungry, grief, rough (sleeping out), child (one of theirs ill);
#             aches and hurts need no key: the everyday answers fit illness, aches and knocks alike. The answers
#             for tired, hungry, grief, rough and child have the say alone (no health.back). The everyday answers
#             remember their stance (pair.mem.ha = advice, kind, rough, pup) and the last word suits it.
#   memories: pair.mem.mk = grief (ended with the answer), home (missing where they grew up); a pup's memories are
#             answered as a pup's (e3_ma_they_young); only those past being pups say "when I was young".

# ================================================================ Health: one speaks of their own

rule e3_hr_open
when concept=talk.health
say I'm not right today. Can't say what. | Something's going round and I think it found me. | My stomach's been at me since breakfast. | I've a head on me like a bell being rung.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

rule e3_hr_open_chill
when concept=talk.health
say I think I've caught #chill#. | My nose has been running like a tap since Restday. | I'm feeling #poorly#, if I'm honest. | I've a cough that's settled in like a lodger.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

rule e3_hr_open_crick
when concept=talk.health
say I've a crick in my neck from sleeping wrong. | I've done something to my back. Bent for a bucket and it went. | My shoulder's stiff as a board this morning.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_open_sleep
when concept=talk.health tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say I've not slept properly in a week. | Woke at the third bell and lay there till dawn. | I dreamt all night and woke more #tired# than I went to bed.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=tired 2m

rule e3_hr_old
when concept=talk.health stage=old
cooldown 2d
say My knees are telling me about the weather again. | I've a new ache. I'd run out of the old ones. | Took me half the morning to get my boots on. | My paws won't close in the mornings any more.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d

rule e3_hr_old_teeth
when concept=talk.health stage=old
cooldown 2d
say I've four teeth left and two of them are thinking about it. | Everything I eat now has to be soup. | My hearing's going. What? Exactly.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_young
when concept=talk.health stage=young
cooldown 1d
say I've got a tummy ache. Can I have honey? | My tooth's wobbly and it hurts when I eat. | I fell over and grazed my knee. I didn't even cry.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_hurt_light
when concept=talk.health injured=light
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Took a knock. It's #hurt#, but it'll mend. | Mind my arm. It's bruised black under the fur. | Twisted my paw. Walking like a crab.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d

rule e3_hr_hurt_bad
when concept=talk.health injured=bad
priority 2
cooldown 12h
say I'm in a bad way. I won't pretend I'm not. | Every breath hurts. | I need to sit. I need to sit down.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d

rule e3_hr_tired
when concept=talk.health tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say I'm so #tired# my fur aches. | If I sit down I won't get up. | I could sleep on a fence post.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=tired 2m

rule e3_hr_hungry
when concept=talk.health hungry=yes
cooldown 1d
say I'm light-headed. Haven't eaten. | My belly's growling louder than I talk. | I came over dizzy at the well. I've had nothing since yesterday.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=hungry 2m

rule e3_hr_mourning
when concept=talk.health mourning=kin|friend
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I can't eat. I can't sleep. It's not the body, it's the rest. | There's a weight on my chest since the burial. | I'm all hollow inside. Is that a sickness?
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=grief 2m

rule e3_hr_homeless
when concept=talk.health homeless=yes
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Sleeping in doorways. My bones have frozen through. | You get a cough you can't shift, sleeping out. | My paws haven't been warm in a week.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=rough 2m

rule e3_hr_parent
when concept=talk.health parent=yes
cooldown 2d
say One of mine's been up all night with a cough. So have I. | The little ones have spots. All of them. | One of mine has a fever. I've not left the bedside since yesterday.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=child 2m

rule e3_hr_poor
when concept=talk.health wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say I've a pain I can't afford to have looked at. | The healer's for them that can pay. I'll wait it out. | I could do with a draught but it's that or supper.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d

rule e3_hr_rich
when concept=talk.health wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say My physician says I'm to avoid excitement and rich food. | I've been taking the waters. Dreadful taste. | I've had a slight chill. The whole household's been in uproar.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_nervy
when concept=talk.health temper=nervy
cooldown 1d
say I've a lump. Here. Is it a lump? Feel it. No, don't. | I think my heart skipped. Twice. | There's a fever two doors down. I'll be next, I know it.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

rule e3_hr_short
when concept=talk.health temper=short
cooldown 1d
say I've a cough and everyone keeps telling me about it. | The healer says rest. I said I'd rest when she pays my rent. | Don't ask about my back.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_devout
when concept=talk.health piety=devout
cooldown 2d
say My cough's no better. I've prayed on it. | I've had a fever. I've offered it up. | The gods send aches to remind us we're only lent our bodies. I've been reminded this week.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

rule e3_hr_merry
when concept=talk.health humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say I'm dying. Slowly. Over about forty years. | The healer took one look at my tongue and asked for paying first. | I sneezed so hard I saw my grandmother.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_miner
when concept=talk.health job=miner
cooldown 2d
say Coughing up the seam again. | My chest's full of rock dust. Every miner's is. | The damp down there gets into your knees.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d

rule e3_hr_smith
when concept=talk.health job=smith
cooldown 2d
say Caught a spark on the wrist. Another one. | My ears ring from the anvil all night. | The heat's dried me out like a smoked fish.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_farmer
when concept=talk.health job=farmer|herder
cooldown 2d
say My back's bent like a scythe from the rows. | Kicked by a cow. Same cow as last week. | Scythe nicked my shin. Bled like a pig.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_fisher
when concept=talk.health job=fisher|sailor
cooldown 2d
say Salt water's cracked my pads to the bone. | My paws won't straighten after a night on the nets. | I've been wet so long I'm growing moss.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_guard
when concept=talk.health job=guard|soldier
cooldown 2d
say My feet are ruined from standing watch. | The armour's rubbed me raw under the arm. | Got clipped in training. My ear's still ringing.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_labour
when concept=talk.health job=laborer|carter|woodcutter
cooldown 2d
say Shoulders like knotted rope. | Every rut in the road went up my spine. | Pulled something lifting. Something important.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_healer
when concept=talk.health job=healer
cooldown 2d
say I've caught everyone's cold at once. Healer, heal thyself. | Up all night with a fever case. Mine now, I think. | I've seen fifty patients this week. I'd like to be one.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

rule e3_hr_cook
when concept=talk.health job=cook|baker
cooldown 2d
say Burned my paw on the oven door again. | Flour in my lungs. I sneeze bread. | Stood at the hearth all day. My feet are cooked.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_winter
when concept=talk.health here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say I've chilblains on every toe. | This cold's got into my chest. | The whole street's got the winter fever, and now so have I.
then other: health.answer
remember self: e3_ailing 3d

rule e3_hr_summer
when concept=talk.health here.season=summer
cooldown 1d
say This heat's making me sick. Can't keep anything down. | Burned my nose in the sun. | I'm panting like I've run here from the next town, and I've only crossed the street.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_damp
when concept=talk.health here.weather=rain|fog|storm
cooldown 1d
say This damp's in my joints. | The wet's gone to my chest again. | My fur hasn't been dry in a week. I'll go mouldy.
then other: health.answer

rule e3_hr_ridgemere
when concept=talk.health here.region=ridgemere here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
cooldown 2d
say It's the Ridgemere cough. Everyone has it. | This city's air is half sea, half chimney. | I wheeze from the wharf to the Heights.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

rule e3_hr_quirk_storm
when concept=talk.health quirk=sleeps_badly_before_storms
cooldown 1d
say Storm's coming. I didn't sleep a wink. | My fur's crackling. Didn't sleep. Storm by dark.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=tired 2m

rule e3_hr_quirk_cough
when concept=talk.health quirk=coughs_in_the_damp_and_pretends_not_to
cooldown 1d
say *coughs* I'm perfectly well. | Never better. *coughs* Never better.
then other: health.answer
remember pair: hk=sick 2m

## Asking after it, days later (the ailing one is remembered)

rule e3_hr_ask_after
when concept=talk.health other.mem.e3_ailing pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family|spouses
priority 1
cooldown 3d
say Are you any better? You weren't well, last I saw you. | How's whatever it was? Mended? | You were #poorly#. Better now?
then other: keeping.answer

# ================================================================ Health: the other answers, as they are
# The everyday answers fit a sickness, an ache or a knock alike.

rule e3_ha_plain
when concept=health.answer
say Sorry to hear it. | That's no good. | Poor you. | Well, look after yourself.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_remedy
when concept=health.answer
say Have you tried #remedy#? | #remedy.capitalize#. Works every time. | My mother would have said #remedy#.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_healer
when concept=health.answer job=healer
priority 2
say Come by and I'll look at it. Don't leave it. | Rest, warmth and nothing stupid. I know. Nobody does it. | Show me later. Before it's worse, not after.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_priest
when concept=health.answer job=priest
priority 1
say I'll remember you at the evening prayer. | Come to the chapel. Sit a while. The body follows the heart. | The gods mend slowly, but they mend.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_devout
when concept=health.answer piety=devout
cooldown 12h
say I'll pray for you. | Light a candle. It can't hurt. | The gods see it. They'll see you through.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_old
when concept=health.answer stage=old other.stage!=old
cooldown 1d
say You think that's bad? Wait till you're my age. | Pfft. I've had that since before you were born. | You young ones. One ache and it's the end of the world.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=rough 2m

rule e3_ha_old_plain
when concept=health.answer stage=old
cooldown 12h
say Ah, I know that one well. | I've had the same, on and off, for years. | Rest it. I never did, and look at me.
then other: health.back

rule e3_ha_young
when concept=health.answer stage=young
say Does it hurt? Can I see? | #mum# says you have to have soup when you're poorly. | Are you going to die?
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=pup 2m

rule e3_ha_nervy
when concept=health.answer temper=nervy
cooldown 12h
say Don't come too close. Not that I mind. I do mind. | My cousin had something like that and he went yellow. | You should go to the healer. Now. Today.
then other: health.back

rule e3_ha_short
when concept=health.answer temper=short
cooldown 12h
say Stop moaning and see the healer. | We've all got something. | Then go home. Don't stand there telling me.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=rough 2m

rule e3_ha_warm
when concept=health.answer warmth=warm
cooldown 12h
say I'll bring you some broth tonight. | Come and sit by my fire. | Oh, #pet#. You need looking after.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_cold
when concept=health.answer warmth=cold
cooldown 12h
say Mm. | Everyone's got something. | I'm sure it'll pass.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=rough 2m

rule e3_ha_merry
when concept=health.answer humour=merry
cooldown 12h
say Can I have your boots if you don't pull through? | You'll live. Unfortunately for the rest of us. | That's what comes of being so good-looking.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=rough 2m

rule e3_ha_dry
when concept=health.answer humour=dry
cooldown 12h
say Well, you've looked worse. Not much. | Could be worse. Could be me. | And here's me thinking you were made of iron.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=rough 2m

rule e3_ha_sly
when concept=health.answer honesty=sly
cooldown 12h
say I know a carter sells a tonic. Very reasonable. I could get you some. | The healer overcharges. I've something at home. For a penny. | Don't go to the healer. Come to me.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_chatty
when concept=health.answer talk=chatty
cooldown 12h
say My cousin had that. Three weeks. Then it went to her ears, then her feet. Then she was fine. | Oh, I had that! Started in the toes, it did. | Funny you say, there's a wolf on our street, same thing.
then other: health.back

rule e3_ha_poor
when concept=health.answer wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 12h
say Healers are for them with money. Sleep it off. | Same as me. You get better or you don't. | Hot water and salt. It's what we've got.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_rich
when concept=health.answer wealth=rich
cooldown 12h
say You should see my physician. He's very good. | Have you thought of a week by the sea? | Oh, you poor thing. Have your cook make you a broth.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_cook
when concept=health.answer job=cook|baker
say Broth. Bone broth. I'll put a pot on. | Nothing a good stew won't mend. | You're not eating right. I can tell.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_drink
when concept=health.answer job=innkeeper|brewer
say A drop of brandy. Medicinal. | Come by tonight. Hot ale with honey. On the house. Well, half. | Nothing a cup won't ease.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_herder
when concept=health.answer job=herder|farmer
cooldown 12h
say I'd give a ewe a warm mash and a dry bed for that. Same for you. | Work it off. That's what I do. | Goose grease. I swear by it for the beasts.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

rule e3_ha_parent
when concept=health.answer parent=yes
cooldown 12h
say I'd tell my pups bed and soup. You're no different. | You sound just like my youngest. Same whine. | My mother's cure: onion in a sock. Don't ask.
then other: health.back

rule e3_ha_miner
when concept=health.answer job=miner
cooldown 12h
say You should try a shift underground. Then talk to me. | That's nothing. Come and hear my chest some morning. | Pfft. Rock falls on you, that's hurt.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=rough 2m

rule e3_ha_spouses
when concept=health.answer pair.band=spouses
say Bed. Now. I'll bring you something hot. | Why didn't you wake me? | That's it. You're not going out today.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_friends
when concept=health.answer pair.band=friends|family
cooldown 12h
say Why didn't you come to me? | You should have said. I'll come by tonight. | Let me look at you. #oath#, you look rough.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_they_bad
when concept=health.answer other.injured=bad
priority 3
say #oath#, sit down before you fall down. | You need the healer. I'll take you. | Don't talk. Lean on me.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

rule e3_ha_they_old
when concept=health.answer other.stage=old
cooldown 12h
say You should rest more, at your age. | Sit down. I'll fetch whatever you need. | My grandmother swore by a hot brick in a cloth.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=advice 2m

# A pup's tummy, tooth or knee: answered as a pup's, by whoever isn't one.
rule e3_ha_they_young
when concept=health.answer other.stage=young self.stage!=young
priority 3
say Brave pup. It'll be better by tomorrow. | Go and tell your #mum#. They'll know what to do. | Show me. Ooh. Very brave. Honey for that, I'd say.
then other: health.back

rule e3_ha_same
when concept=health.answer self.mem.e3_ailing pair.mem.hk=sick
priority 1
say You too? I've had the same all week. | It's going round. I've got it as well. | Snap. We'll be ill together.
then other: health.back
remember pair: ha=kind 2m

# Worn out (hk=tired): the say is theirs.
rule e3_ha_tired
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=tired
priority 3
say Then go to bed, you daft thing. | Get some sleep. The work'll be there tomorrow. | You look it. No offence.

rule e3_ha_tired_warm
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=tired warmth=warm
priority 2
say Sit. I'll make you something hot, then you're going home. | Put your feet up at mine for an hour. I'll not tell a soul. | Oh, you poor thing. Off to bed with you.

rule e3_ha_tired_merry
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=tired humour=merry
priority 2
say You look like you've been dragged backwards through a hedge. Twice. | Sleep standing up. Horses manage it. | I'll wake you when there's something worth seeing.

rule e3_ha_tired_old
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=tired stage=old
priority 2
say Sleep while you can. At my age it doesn't come. | When I was your age I slept like a stone. Now I count the beams. | Rest. Nobody thanks you for wearing yourself out.

rule e3_ha_tired_young
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=tired stage=young
priority 2
say I don't ever want to sleep. Sleep's boring. | You can have a nap! I'll keep watch. | You yawned! You did it again!

# Hungry (hk=hungry).
rule e3_ha_hungry
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=hungry
priority 4
say Here. Half a loaf. Take it, go on. | Sit down before you fall down. When did you last eat? | You'll eat with us tonight. No arguing.

rule e3_ha_hungry_poor
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=hungry wealth=poor|destitute
priority 3
say I've nothing myself, or I'd share it. You know I would. | The chapel gives out bread at dawn. Get there early. | Here. It's only a crust, but it's yours.

rule e3_ha_hungry_rich
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=hungry wealth=rich
priority 3
say Good heavens. Here, buy yourself a hot pie. | That won't do. Take this and get something proper. | Go round to my kitchen door. Tell them I sent you.

rule e3_ha_hungry_cook
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=hungry job=cook|baker|innkeeper
priority 3
say Come round the back. There's always something. | I've yesterday's loaves going spare. Have the lot. | Sit. I'll bring you a bowl. You can pay me another day.

rule e3_ha_hungry_cold
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=hungry warmth=cold
priority 3
say We all go short sometimes. | Then you'd best find some work. | Mm. That's hard.

rule e3_ha_hungry_young
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=hungry stage=young
priority 3
say You can have my crust. I'm not hungry. Much. | #mum# always has bread. Come home with me! | I've got an apple. Half each?

# Grieving (hk=grief).
rule e3_ha_grief
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=grief
priority 5
say It's not something you mend. You carry it, and it gets lighter. | Of course you can't. Nobody would expect you to. | Grief's a sickness of its own. Be gentle with yourself.

rule e3_ha_grief_warm
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=grief warmth=warm
priority 4
say Come and sit with us tonight. You shouldn't be alone. | Oh, #pet#. Come here. | I'll bring something round. You'll not have to cook.

rule e3_ha_grief_devout
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=grief piety=devout
priority 4
say They're in the Bright One's keeping now. Let that be a little comfort. | I'll pray for them, and for you. | Come to the chapel with me. Just to sit.

rule e3_ha_grief_old
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=grief stage=old
priority 4
say It never goes. But it gets lighter to carry. I promise you that. | I've buried more than I can count. It's always like this, at first. | Eat something anyway. They'd want you to.

rule e3_ha_grief_cold
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=grief warmth=cold
priority 4
say It passes. Slowly, but it does. | We all lose someone. | I'm sorry. I'm no good with these things.

rule e3_ha_grief_young
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=grief stage=young
priority 4
say Are you sad? I'll be quiet with you. | I can sit with you. I'm good at sitting. | #mum# says the ones we lose go to the Bright One.

# Sleeping out (hk=rough).
rule e3_ha_rough
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=rough
priority 4
say There's a bed at the chapel, some nights. Go early. | Keep out of the wind and keep moving, or you'll not wake. | Come by the back door tonight. There's a corner by the stove.

rule e3_ha_rough_warm
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=rough warmth=warm
priority 3
say Sleep in my shed tonight. I mean it. It's dry, at least. | You'll have my old coat. I'll not hear no. | Come to ours. We'll squeeze up.

rule e3_ha_rough_rich
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=rough wealth=rich
priority 3
say Dreadful. Someone really ought to do something. | Here. Get a bed at an inn tonight. | The Council should see to it. I'll mention it.

rule e3_ha_rough_poor
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=rough wealth=poor|destitute
priority 3
say I know. I've slept in a few doorways myself. | Find a stable. The beasts keep it warm. | Stick together. Two's warmer than one.

rule e3_ha_rough_guard
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=rough job=guard
priority 3
say Not in the gateways. I'll have to move you on. Try the chapel porch. | Stay where the lamps are. It's safer. | I'll look the other way at the stables tonight. Once.

# One of theirs ill (hk=child).
rule e3_ha_child
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=child
priority 3
say Poor mite. Keep them warm and give them plenty to drink. | They're tougher than we think, the little ones. | Every house on the street's had it. It passes.

rule e3_ha_child_parent
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=child parent=yes
priority 2
say Ours had the same last winter. A week of misery and then they were climbing the walls. | Honey and warm milk. And sleep when they sleep. | You'll be the one needing a healer by the end of it.

rule e3_ha_child_healer
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=child job=healer
priority 2
say Bring them by. I'll look at them. No charge. | Keep them warm and watch the fever. If it climbs, come for me. | Sounds like what's going round. I'll call in later.

rule e3_ha_child_old
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=child stage=old
priority 2
say I nursed mine through worse. They come through it. | Spots? Every pup gets spots. You did. | Keep the fire up and the shutters closed. That's all it ever was.

rule e3_ha_child_warm
when concept=health.answer pair.mem.hk=child warmth=warm
priority 2
say I'll send round some broth for them. And for you. | Poor little things. Tell them I asked after them. | Get some sleep yourself. I'll sit with them an hour.

# ================================================================ Health: the last word (after the everyday answers)

rule e3_hb_plain
when concept=health.back
say I'll live. | It'll pass. | #saying#. | We'll see.

rule e3_hb_advice
when concept=health.back pair.mem.ha=advice
say Maybe I will. | I'll try it. | Everyone says that. I might even do it.

rule e3_hb_kind
when concept=health.back pair.mem.ha=kind
say That's good of you. | Thank you. I mean it. | You're kind. I'll be right in a day or two.

rule e3_hb_rough
when concept=health.back pair.mem.ha=rough
say Thank you for your sympathy. | Charming. | I'll remember that when it's you.

rule e3_hb_pup
when concept=health.back pair.mem.ha=pup
priority 1
say No, pup. Not today. | Only a bit. | I'll live, little one.

rule e3_hb_short
when concept=health.back temper=short
say Hmph. | I'll manage. | Enough about it.

rule e3_hb_nervy
when concept=health.back temper=nervy
say You don't think it's serious? Do you? | I'll go and see the healer. Today. | Now I'll not sleep for worrying.

rule e3_hb_merry
when concept=health.back humour=merry
say If I die, I'm haunting you. | Put that on my stone. | I'll live. Out of spite, mostly.

rule e3_hb_devout
when concept=health.back piety=devout
say The gods willing. | It's in better hands than mine. | I'll offer it up tonight.

rule e3_hb_old
when concept=health.back stage=old
say At my age you take what comes. | I've survived worse. I've survived most folk. | Never get old. That's my advice.

rule e3_hb_young
when concept=health.back stage=young
say All right. | Can I have honey, then? | I'm brave. I'm very brave.

rule e3_hb_poor
when concept=health.back wealth=poor|destitute
say I'll manage. We always do. | When I've the coin. | Can't stop working, either way.

rule e3_hb_warm
when concept=health.back warmth=warm
say I'll be all right. Don't you fret. | You're a dear for listening. | I'll be right as rain in a day or two.

rule e3_hb_cold
when concept=health.back warmth=cold
say We'll see. | I'll manage. | It's nothing.

# ================================================================ Memories: one remembers
# Only those past being pups remember being small; a pup's memories are short (e3_mr_young).

rule e3_mr_open
when concept=talk.memories stage!=young
say Funny what comes back to you. I was thinking about my first pair of boots. | I was remembering my grandmother this morning. Out of nowhere. | I passed the old schoolroom today. Still smells of chalk. | I found a wooden top of mine at the back of a chest. It still spins.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: e3_reminisced 3d

rule e3_mr_open_smell
when concept=talk.memories stage!=young
say The smell of bread always takes me back to my mother's kitchen. | I heard a fiddle tune yesterday and I was ten again. | Somebody laughed in the street like my father used to. Stopped me cold.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: e3_reminisced 3d

rule e3_mr_open_town
when concept=talk.memories stage!=young
say They say there used to be a well right here, before anyone's time. | That window, there. I courted under it one whole summer. Never got a word out of her. | When I was small, every street was #mud#. Look at it now.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_old
when concept=talk.memories stage=old
cooldown 2d
say The winters were harder when I was young. Snow up to the shutters. | Bread was better then. Real crust on it. | In my day we walked everywhere, and we were glad of it. | I remember the old lord. Rode a white horse. Nobody since has looked so grand.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: e3_reminisced 3d

rule e3_mr_old_love
when concept=talk.memories stage=old
cooldown 2d
say I was thinking about my first sweetheart. #oath#, the ears on that one. | I can still see the hat my first sweetheart wore to the spring dance. Awful hat. I loved it. | Did I tell you I nearly married a miller? I'd have been fat and happy.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_old_plague
when concept=talk.memories stage=old
cooldown 3d
say I lived through the Grey Year. The sickness. Half the street. | I remember the great flood. My mother put us up on the roof. | The year of the hungry spring, we ate bark soup.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_young
when concept=talk.memories stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Last summer I found a bird's egg! A blue one! | When I was little I was scared of goats. | Remember yesterday? I was so fast. Nobody could catch me.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_adolescent
when concept=talk.memories stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say When I was a pup I thought I'd be a knight. | I used to think the priest could see through walls. | Everything was easier when I was small.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_widowed
when concept=talk.memories widowed=yes
cooldown 1d
say I keep turning to say "#dear#, look at that", and nobody's there. | All those years married, and I still hear the door and think it's them. | I found one of their old gloves in the chest. Sat with it all evening.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=grief 2m

rule e3_mr_mourning
when concept=talk.memories mourning=kin|friend
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I keep remembering things they said. Silly things. | The last time I saw them, they were laughing. | I'd give anything for one more ordinary day with them.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=grief 2m

rule e3_mr_friends
when concept=talk.memories pair.band=friends pair.familiarity>=50
cooldown 1d
say Remember when we tried to sail to the end of the world in a washtub? Your idea. | Remember the night we sang under the miller's window? You sang flat. | Remember when you fell out of the apple tree and blamed me?
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: e3_shared 30m
remember pair: e3_reminisced 3d

rule e3_mr_close
when concept=talk.memories pair.band=friends pair.familiarity>=40
cooldown 2d
say You're the only one who remembers me as I was. | I was thinking about the day we met. I remember every bit of it. | We've seen a lot, you and me.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_family
when concept=talk.memories pair.kin=siblings
cooldown 1d
say #mum# burnt the pancakes every Restday, remember? On purpose, she said. | The old house. The roof leaked over your bed, not mine. | Remember when we hid in the hayloft all afternoon and they had the whole street out looking?
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: e3_shared 30m

rule e3_mr_spouses
when concept=talk.memories pair.band=spouses
cooldown 1d
say I was thinking about the day we wed. It rained on everyone but us. | Our first winter, we had one blanket and one chair. I'd not trade it. | You used to leave flowers on the step. Before you got lazy.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: e3_shared 30m

rule e3_mr_again
when concept=talk.memories pair.mem.e3_reminisced
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Since we talked about the old days, it keeps coming back to me. | I remembered something else, after we spoke. | You set me off, the other day. I've been remembering all week.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_from_frost
when concept=talk.memories from=frosthollow here.region!=frosthollow
cooldown 2d
say I miss the snow, would you believe it. The proper deep stuff. | Back home in the valley the pines creak all winter. I can't sleep without it. | Up in Frosthollow we'd sing in the dark to keep warm.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_from_coldwater
when concept=talk.memories from=coldwater here.region!=coldwater
cooldown 2d
say I miss the lake. Clear as air, the Glasswater. | We'd swim out to the island every summer. I still dream of it. | Back home the mist on the lake in the morning was like milk.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_from_oakhaven
when concept=talk.memories from=oakhaven here.region!=oakhaven
cooldown 2d
say We used to sleep out under the oaks on hot nights. I miss the sound of the leaves. | In the Warmwood we knew every oak by its name. | The woods after rain. I'd give a week's #wages# to smell that.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_from_mirebridge
when concept=talk.memories from=mirebridge here.region!=mirebridge
cooldown 2d
say I miss the fen at dusk. The frogs starting up, the mist coming in over the reeds. | Back home, the frogs sang all night. It's too quiet here. | My mother could read the fen mist like a book.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_from_larkfield
when concept=talk.memories from=larkfield here.region!=larkfield
cooldown 2d
say I miss the downs. All that sky and the larks going up. | The wind on the downs. I can't sleep without something rattling the shutters. | #dad# used to take me up the hill at dawn to watch the larks go up.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_from_southmeadow
when concept=talk.memories from=southmeadow here.region!=southmeadow
cooldown 2d
say I miss the orchards. Blossom like snow, but warm. | Back home we'd eat plums off the tree till we were sick. | I haven't been properly warm since I left the south.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_from_city
when concept=talk.memories from=ridgemere here.region=towns
cooldown 2d
say I grew up in Ridgemere. I miss the bells. And the noise, oddly. | When I came out from the city, I'd never seen a cow up close. | In the city you're never alone. Out here you're never anything else.
then other: memories.answer
remember pair: mk=home 2m

rule e3_mr_ridgemere_old
when concept=talk.memories here.region=ridgemere stage=old
cooldown 2d
say When I was a pup there were fields where the suburbs are. | I remember when the Rainrun had no bridge. You waded, or you swam. | I remember the wharf when it was half the length, and the old Greatly lord walking it every morning.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_town_old
when concept=talk.memories here.region=towns stage=old
cooldown 2d
say I miss the old mill. The whole town smelled of flour on grinding days. | There used to be a dance every Restday eve, before the hall burned. | The crossroads was all grass when I was small. We kept geese on it.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_chatty
when concept=talk.memories talk=chatty stage!=young
cooldown 1d
say My aunt once chased a runaway pig the length of the town in her nightgown. Caught it, too. | When I was a pup there was a wolf on our street kept seven cats, and named every one of them Duchess. | You'll never guess who I was thinking about. Old Tamsin! The one with the goats!
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_content
when concept=talk.memories drive=content stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say I had a happy childhood. I don't think I knew it then. | Some afternoons, years ago, I'd live again just as they were. | I remember sitting on a wall in the sun with an apple. Nothing else. Perfect.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_frank
when concept=talk.memories honesty=frank stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say People say the old days were better. They weren't. They were colder and hungrier. | My childhood was hard and I'll not dress it up. | I don't miss being young. I was a fool.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_merry
when concept=talk.memories humour=merry stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say When I was a pup I tried to marry the priest's goat. | I once fell asleep in a hay cart and woke up in another town. | My brother and I painted the miller's pig. Blue.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_devout
when concept=talk.memories piety=devout stage!=young
cooldown 2d
say The old priest used to give every pup a honey cake after the blessing. | My mother took us to chapel in the snow. Every Restday. Never missed. | I sang in the chapel as a pup. Off key, but loud. The Bright One didn't seem to mind.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_rich
when concept=talk.memories wealth=rich job!=noble
cooldown 3d
say People forget I started with a barrow and a borrowed coat. | My father mended boots by candlelight. I've not forgotten. | My first shop was a plank on two barrels.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_noble
when concept=talk.memories job=noble stage!=young
cooldown 3d
say My governess made me recite every House's lineage before breakfast. I can still do it. | I was nine before I knew other pups didn't have their own pony. | My grandfather took me round the estate on his saddle and said, all this will need minding. It does.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_poor
when concept=talk.memories wealth=poor|destitute stage!=young
cooldown 3d
say We had a proper house once. Before things went wrong. | There was a time I had two coats and didn't think about it. | I used to give pennies to beggars. Funny, that.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_soldier
when concept=talk.memories job=guard|soldier stage=adult|old
cooldown 3d
say I remember the bandit winter. We held the gate a fortnight. | My first watch, I challenged a scarecrow. Twice. | The old captain could shout the birds out of the trees.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_festival
when concept=talk.memories here.day=festival
cooldown 1d
say I danced my first dance at this festival. Trod on everyone. | My father used to lift me up on his shoulders to see the fire. | This festival always smells the same. Smoke and honey cakes. Every year.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_winter
when concept=talk.memories here.season=winter
cooldown 2d
say First snow always takes me back. Snowball wars, our street against the next. | We'd tell stories round the fire all winter when I was small. | I remember the winter we had to dig out the front door.
then other: memories.answer

rule e3_mr_quirk_story
when concept=talk.memories quirk=tells_the_same_three_stories
cooldown 1d
say Did I ever tell you about the night the miller's cart lost a wheel? Flour from one end of the street to the other. | Have I told you about my uncle and the bear? He ran one way, the bear ran the other. Both of them told it for years.
then other: memories.answer

# ================================================================ Memories: the other answers, as they are

rule e3_ma_plain
when concept=memories.answer
say That takes me back. | Funny what sticks. | Mine was much the same, near enough. | I'd forgotten all about that sort of thing. | You should write these down.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_old
when concept=memories.answer stage=old other.stage!=old
cooldown 1d
say That's nothing. You should have seen it in my day. | Ah. I remember further back than that. | You don't know old days. I know old days.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_old_plain
when concept=memories.answer stage=old
cooldown 12h
say Ah. Now there's a thing I'd forgotten. | It all comes back, doesn't it? All of it. | We all had that, in our day.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_young
when concept=memories.answer stage=young
say That was before I was born, I bet. | I bet there were dragons then. | That's so long ago.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_adolescent
when concept=memories.answer stage=adolescent
say Everyone old says that. | Everything's always better when you were small. | You're not that old.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_shared
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.e3_shared
priority 1
say That's not how it went at all. | You've got it backwards, as usual. | That's not how I remember it. Not even close.
then other: memories.argue
remember pair: e3_reminisced 3d

rule e3_ma_shared_fond
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.e3_shared
priority 1
say I remember. I'll always remember. | #oath#, we were young. | We were, weren't we.
then other: memories.back
remember pair: e3_reminisced 3d

rule e3_ma_friends
when concept=memories.answer pair.band=friends
cooldown 12h
say You never told me that before. | I'd forgotten that one. It's a good one. | I don't believe a word of it. Tell it again.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_frank
when concept=memories.answer honesty=frank
cooldown 12h
say You're remembering it kinder than it was. | It was never that rosy. Nothing was. | Old days were mostly #mud#.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_short
when concept=memories.answer temper=short
cooldown 12h
say Must we? Some of us have work. | Old news. | That was then. This is now, and I'm busy.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_warm
when concept=memories.answer warmth=warm
cooldown 12h
say Tell me more. I like hearing it. | That's lovely. Really. | I wish I'd known you then.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_cold
when concept=memories.answer warmth=cold
cooldown 12h
say I don't think about the past much. | Mm. | That was then.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_dry
when concept=memories.answer humour=dry
cooldown 12h
say And now look at you. | Ah, the good old days. When we were miserable and didn't know it. | They weren't old then. They were just days.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_merry
when concept=memories.answer humour=merry
cooldown 12h
say Ha! That's the best thing I've heard all week. | Ha! Now that I believe. | You were a terror, I bet. You still are.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_devout
when concept=memories.answer piety=devout
cooldown 12h
say The gods kept us through all of it. | We should give thanks for the years. | Remember them in your prayers. I do mine.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_chatty
when concept=memories.answer talk=chatty
cooldown 12h
say That reminds me, my uncle once... no, you tell yours first. | Oh, and there was the fellow with the goats. I'll tell you that one after. | We had one just like that! I'll tell you after.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_quiet
when concept=memories.answer talk=quiet
cooldown 12h
say Mm. I remember. | Aye. | ... Good times.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_elsewhere
when concept=memories.answer pair.same_from=no
cooldown 12h
say Where I grew up, it was different. | We had nothing like that at home. | Sounds just like home, and nothing like it.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_same_place
when concept=memories.answer pair.same_from=yes
cooldown 12h
say Same as at home. Same as us. | I know. We grew up on the same #mud#. | Same place, same winters.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_widowed
when concept=memories.answer widowed=yes
cooldown 12h
say My late mate used to say just that. | I'd tell mine that, if mine were here. | I remember too much, these days.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_mourning
when concept=memories.answer mourning=kin|friend
priority 1
say Don't. Not today. I can't. | We buried someone this week. Remembering hurts just now. | I'll laugh at that another day.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_poor
when concept=memories.answer wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 12h
say Some of us can't afford to look back. Too far to fall. | I'd rather remember than think about now. | The past was cheaper.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_forward
when concept=memories.answer drive=ambitious|restless
cooldown 12h
say I'd rather look forward. | The past's done. What's next? | Old days. I want new ones.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_quirk_names
when concept=memories.answer quirk=remembers_every_name_ever_heard
say And the wolf next door was Hobb. Hobb Fennick. Wore a red cap. | I remember the names of everyone in it. Shall I list them? | Bramble. That was the goat's name. Bramble.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_quirk_sayings
when concept=memories.answer quirk=quotes_old_sayings_for_everything
say As they say, the old days are the ones we lived through. | Old saying: you can't go home, but you can visit. | My grandmother said a wolf who forgets is a wolf twice bitten.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_they_old
when concept=memories.answer other.stage=old
cooldown 12h
say Tell me more. Nobody tells it like you. | I wish I'd seen it. | They don't make days like that any more.
then other: memories.back

# A pup's memory (last summer, yesterday), answered as a pup's.
rule e3_ma_they_young
when concept=memories.answer other.stage=young self.stage!=young
priority 3
say That long ago, eh? | You'll remember that all your life. | Ha! And look at you now.
then other: memories.back

# Missing where they grew up (mk=home).
rule e3_ma_home
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=home
priority 2
say You'll go back one day, I'd bet. | It sounds a fine place to have come from. | I'd like to see it, some day.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_home_same
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=home pair.same_from=yes
priority 1
say I miss it too. Every day. | I'd forgotten that. Now I'll be homesick all week. | Don't. You'll set me off.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_home_old
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=home stage=old
priority 1
say You never stop missing it. You only get used to the missing. | Home's where you were young. Can't go back to that, wherever you walk. | Go and see it, while you've the legs.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_home_dry
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=home humour=dry
priority 1
say And yet here you are. | Strange how home's always better from a distance. | I'll help you pack.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_home_frank
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=home honesty=frank
priority 1
say It'll have changed. Places do, when you're not looking. | Then why did you leave it? No, don't tell me. I know why. | Missing it's easier than living there, I'd guess.
then other: memories.back

rule e3_ma_home_warm
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=home warmth=warm
priority 1
say Then you'll tell me all about it, some evening. I'd love that. | It's in your voice when you talk of it. | We'll have to make this place feel more like home for you.
then other: memories.back

# Grief (mk=grief): the answer has the say alone.
rule e3_ma_grief
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=grief
priority 5
say Keep remembering. It's how they stay. | Of course you do. You'd not be you if you didn't. | That's the hard part. The ordinary things.

rule e3_ma_grief_warm
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=grief warmth=warm
priority 4
say Oh, #pet#. Come here. | Tell me about them, whenever you like. Any time at all. | I'm here. Whenever it comes over you, I'm here.

rule e3_ma_grief_devout
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=grief piety=devout
priority 4
say The Bright One keeps them now. And you keep the rest. | I'll remember them in my prayers tonight. | They're not so far as they seem.

rule e3_ma_grief_old
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=grief stage=old
priority 4
say It never goes. It gets lighter to carry. | I still hear mine, some mornings. It's a comfort, after a while. | Say their name out loud now and then. It helps.

rule e3_ma_grief_cold
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=grief warmth=cold
priority 4
say It passes. Slowly. | We all lose someone. | I'm sorry. I'm no good at this.

rule e3_ma_grief_young
when concept=memories.answer pair.mem.mk=grief stage=young
priority 4
say I'll sit with you. I'm good at sitting. | Are you sad? You can hold my paw. | I miss people too, sometimes.

# ================================================================ Memories: the last word

rule e3_mb_plain
when concept=memories.back
say Aye. Well. That's how it was. | It all goes by. | Long time ago now. | Doesn't seem so long.

rule e3_mb_old
when concept=memories.back stage=old
say Ah well. All gone now. | It's all I've got, the remembering. | Gone now. Most of it.

rule e3_mb_young
when concept=memories.back stage=young
say It was ages ago. | I'm going to remember it forever. | And then I went home.

rule e3_mb_short
when concept=memories.back temper=short
say Well. There it is. | That's all I'll say about it. | Enough of that.

rule e3_mb_warm
when concept=memories.back warmth=warm
say I'm glad I said it out loud. | It's good to talk about it. | Some things want saying, now and then.

rule e3_mb_merry
when concept=memories.back humour=merry
say And I'd do it all again. | I'd do it again tomorrow, mind. | Ha. Them were the days.

rule e3_mb_frank
when concept=memories.back honesty=frank
say I'm only telling it how it was. | Better or worse, it's true. | I'll not pretend otherwise.

rule e3_mb_quiet
when concept=memories.back talk=quiet
say Mm. | Aye. | ...

rule e3_mb_content
when concept=memories.back drive=content
say Good years. Good years. | I'd not change any of it. | It was enough.

# Friends and family arguing over who remembers it right (after e3_ma_shared): the one who began insists, or gives in.

rule e3_mg_plain
when concept=memories.argue
say It was not! I was there! | You were there too, and you know it. | Fine. Have it your way. It was still you.
then other: memories.settle

rule e3_mg_short
when concept=memories.argue temper=short
say Don't you dare. I know what I saw. | You always do this. Every time. | I'm not having this argument again.
then other: memories.settle

rule e3_mg_merry
when concept=memories.argue humour=merry
say Ha! Liar! You were there and you know it. | Your memory's as bad as your singing. | You'll be telling me next the sky was green.

rule e3_mg_calm
when concept=memories.argue temper=calm
say Maybe. It was a long time ago. | We'll each keep our own version, then. | Have it your way. I know what I remember.

rule e3_mg_old
when concept=memories.argue stage=old
say At my age I remember that better than this morning. | My memory's the only thing that still works. Trust it. | You'll remember I'm right when I'm gone.
then other: memories.settle

rule e3_ms_plain
when concept=memories.settle
say Ha. Same as ever, you. | Let's call it both of us. | We'll ask someone who was there. | Fine. Fine!

rule e3_ms_warm
when concept=memories.settle warmth=warm
say Ha! I've missed this. | Whoever it was, I'm glad it was with you. | Come here, you old fool.

rule e3_ms_short
when concept=memories.settle temper=short
